    "text": "Carbon monoxide is carried around a closed cyclic process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></math>, in which <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;is an isothermal process, as shown in the diagram. The gas absorbs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math> of heat as its temperature is increased from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> in going from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>. The quantity of heat ejected by the gas during the process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0026842_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 151px; height: 152px;\" />",
